[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=PARAMETERS:\\Feedback_Type: Use Percent or Use Time (see progress||1
  Cmn2=meter description below)\\Source_Correction_Wait_Time: The time||1
  Cmn3=to wait after the display has finished warming to send an input||1
  Cmn4=command to try and correct the input if it is incorrect. \\\\INPUTS\\
  Cmn5=Correct_Input_Fb: tie this to the correct feedback for the source||1
  Cmn6=you want the display to be on.\\Warming_Fb: tie this into a warming||1
  Cmn7=fb from a projector\\Cooling_Fb: tie this into a cooling fb from||1
  Cmn8=a projector \\\\Power_On/Off_Press: tie this into a dedicated PowerOn/Off||1
  Cmn9=button from a touchpanel (eliminates the need for an OR symbol and||1
  Cmn10=makes things cleaner)\\\\Power_On/Off_Fb: tie this to the feedback||1
  Cmn11=from whatever display/projector module you are using.\\\\Display_Source:
  Cmn12=||1tie this to the source selection from the touchpanel, not FB from||1
  Cmn13=a video switcher (this wont always change on source selection so||1
  Cmn14=the display/projector wont fire on)\\\\OUTPUTS\\\\Progress_Meter:
  Cmn15=||1a value to denote progress, either 0-100% for either cooling or||1
  Cmn16=warming progress, or it will denote the seconds left until the action||1
  Cmn17=(either warming or cooling) is complete.\\\\	NOTE: this value is||1
  Cmn18=calculated by the actual time it takes the device to warm up or||1
  Cmn19=cool down. the time for warming will be equal to warming time +||1
  Cmn20=the source correction wait time.  \\\\Is_Busy: this signal will||1
  Cmn21=be high while Progress_Meter is ramping\\\\Correct_Input: tie this||1
  Cmn22=to the input you wish to set.\\	NOTE: if Warming_Fb is defined,||1
  Cmn23=this will fire 5s after Warming_Fb goes low. If Warming_Fb is not||1
  Cmn24=defined, it will fire 5s after Power_On_Fb goes high.\\\\Screen_Up/Down:
  Cmn25=||1these will fire when warming starts, and when cooling is finished||1
  Cmn26=to raise the screen.\\\\Power_On/Off: these should be connected||1
  Cmn27=to the inputs on the display/projector module.\\
[END]
